{"parentUuid":"4d8b7d65-94d7-44b5-8070-7a7e0ab024af","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_017yQv4QSzN9ea57hc6Q2Hx5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QDMyByraB45P9uwKQVHDsF","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory/Masterclass/skill/masterclass-builder/SKILL.md","old_string":"## Step 2: Verify facts\n\nSearch for current frameworks, names, numbers, prices, laws, and tools. Replace\nany from-memory claim that could be stale or wrong. This is where most \"expert\nsounding\" course content silently goes false.","new_string":"## Step 2: Deep research and adversarial verification (per module, MANDATORY)\n\nNo module is written from memory. Before drafting each module, run a research\npass deep enough to change at least one belief. Target depth is on the order of\n1,000,000 tokens of genuine research per module, run as a multi-agent fan-out,\nnot one shallow pass. If the finished module says exactly what you would have\nwritten from memory, the research was theater; dig until something surprises you.\n\nThe protocol, run as a multi-agent workflow:\n\n1. **Fan-out web research.** Spawn parallel agents, one per load-bearing claim,\n   framework, name, number, date, price, law, or tool. Each pulls the primary\n   source (the book, the paper, the author's own words), not a blog paraphrase\n   of a paraphrase.\n2. **Source triangulation.** No claim ships on a single source. Cross-reference\n   at least two independent, reputable sources. Quotes are verbatim from the\n   primary source and attributed precisely (author, work, year). A quote you\n   cannot locate in a primary source does not exist; cut it.\n3. **Adversarial verification.** For every load-bearing claim, a separate\n   skeptic agent tries to REFUTE it: wrong attribution, fabricated or misquoted\n   line, overgeneralization, missing caveat, stale number. Default to \"refuted\"\n   when uncertain. A claim ships only if it survives the refutation attempt.\n4. **Steelman the counter-case.** Research the strongest argument AGAINST the\n   module's thesis and the conditions under which it fails. The menu and the\n   traps must reflect it. A one-sided module is a failed module.\n5. **Claim ledger.** Keep a short ledger: each load-bearing claim, its two\n   sources, the verdict, and the surviving caveat. Only ledger-verified claims\n   enter the module. Discard the rest silently; never pad the module with the\n   leftover research.\n\nThis step is where most expert-sounding content silently goes false, and where\nexponential quality comes from: depth of verified research in, density of\ncorrect insight out."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":500,"cache_read_input_tokens":267039,"output_tokens":920,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":500,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":920,"cache_read_input_tokens":267039,"cache_creation_input_tokens":500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":500},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcMFSZrYkBmKYEt3GFpzp","type":"assistant","uuid":"3f054cf8-e01f-4d81-936c-b0d42b03c770","timestamp":"2026-06-24T01:53:28.789Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","sessionId":"31de3be6-4b58-4b16-89fe-eab7c6e76815","version":"2.1.181","gitBranch":"main"}
