ent, an apartment, or food. A comfortable life that leaves time to explore, read, and enjoy.\n- E5. Always include a real marketing and distribution phase; an unseen masterpiece earns nothing.\n- E6. Meaning first: art-first, ownership always, money after; humanity matters more than money alone; he wants world impact. Models: Rockstar, Naughty Dog, Ryu Ga Gotoku (Ichiban), Miyazaki, Kojima.\n\nEngine, risk, body\n\n- E7. Engine: products and IP at the core (packs, tools, a game, courses); freelance only as a capped pocket-money channel with a real strategy; capital for scale later. He is a product and IP profile, introverted, with a strong sense of luxury UI detail.\n- E8. Risk is a barbell: aggressive on the bet and on trying, sober on exposure and frequency. Avoid \"money fast but stressful.\" Onsen and sentō rhythm, never the Yomi Denzel or Oussama Ammar style, his explicit némésis.\n- E9. Health, longevity, sport, sleep, relationships, nutrition are constraints to integrate, never to sacrifice, and must stay compatible with energy-regain rituals (sentō, onsen).\n\nLearner profile\n\n- E10. Skills: 3D, AI, Unreal, Houdini, base Japanese, fluent English, full game design EXCEPT 3D animation and 2D concept art (to learn later, after mastering environment art). Industry-agnostic.\n- E11. Base and ideal environment: Tokyo (Shibuya, Ginza, Roppongi, Toranomon), three to six months a year; doing it in Japan is ideal, not mandatory.\n\nModule format (added by him, emphatic)\n\n- E12. Every module header states estimated reading time AND exercise time, plus position and capability. [enforced by the template]\n- E13. At least one model answer per exercise, so he can self-check. [enforced]\n- E14. \"Lexique express\": one-to-three-word definitions for any term he may not have, maximum precision. [enforced]\n- E15. Run a re-reading and polish pass for maximum intelligence and density before delivering. [enforced by Step 2 and the audit]\n\nProcess and cadence\n\n- E16. ONE module per \"go.\" Never several at once. He says \"go\", you produce one, and you stop. (Stated twice, in capitals.)\n- E17. Sommaire first, then modules one at a time, carrying ALL prior feedback forward cumulatively.\n- E18. Identify the concepts point by point; 80/20 syllabus genuinely useful for his end goals; about 90 minutes per module, extensible to roughly 20 hours total.\n- E19. Separate the work into clear steps; ask only the single decisive, un-defaultable question when truly blocked, never a questionnaire.\n- E20. On request, re-explain any concept more simply in at most three paragraphs plus one recap table (the \"freedom number\" pattern).\n- E21. Each module is the fruit of deep, multi-agent, adversarial, web-sourced research (Step 2). Quality is density, not length (principle 12)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4703,"cache_read_input_tokens":282732,"output_tokens":6699,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4703,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6699,"cache_read_input_tokens":282732,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4703},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcMFjuCrn4GHkk3TqVXM8","type":"assistant","uuid":"3277f80b-3a80-4843-ae51-eedcef7238b7","timestamp":"2026-06-24T01:58:42.414Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory/Masterclass/source","sessionId":"31de3be6-4b58-4b16-89fe-eab7c6e76815","version":"2.1.181","gitBranch":"main"}
