often recurring revenue).\n\n## Brian Casel's Role in Popularizing the Concept\n\nThe idea was popularised by entrepreneurs such as Brian Casel and Dan Norris. They recognised that standardisation not only creates efficiency, but also builds trust.\n\nCasel came to this model through his own experience. Brian realised a service-based business was not conducive to the life he wanted. He believed that products might be the answer. However, SaaS products take a long time to generate sustainable revenue, and he didn't want to waste any more time. Which is where productised services came into play. He realised he could take a service that he was already offering, and then market and price it like a product.\n\n## Key Characteristics\n\nFrom the customer's perspective, they're essentially paying you to do a particular job; but you are in some ways decoupling the hours worked from the service itself. So, you're no longer billing by the hour; you're billing for the project itself. The idea involves selling something that companies need on a repeated recurring basis and then building a process and team."],"durationSeconds":11.175296417000006,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ea5fc34c-7dca-49ec-a8e0-6ce2a9d32173","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","sessionId":"31de3be6-4b58-4b16-89fe-eab7c6e76815","version":"2.1.181","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"a9f30a06-f9bf-43f1-b956-11f8203d4db4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7d537ee-a6e7-4f20-967c-01064d742f22","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QRKwXitnvJTtUKEZmDkc8W","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Rob Walling \"stair step\" approach bootstrapping SaaS steps one-time product\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Rob Walling — Stair-Stepping into SaaS Success – The Bootstrapped Founder\",\"url\":\"https://thebootstrappedfounder.com/rob-walling-stair-stepping-into-saas-success/\"},{\"title\":\"The Stair Step Method of Bootstrapping | Rob Walling\",\"url\":\"https://robwalling.com/essays/2015/03/26/the-stair-step-method-of-bootstrapping\"},{\"title\":\"The Stair Step Method of Bootstrapping by Rob Walling : Garden of Learning by Juhis\",\"url\":\"https://notes.hamatti.org/sources/articles/the-stair-step-method-of-bootstrapping-by-rob-walling\"},{\"title\":\"Walling's Stair Step Method - Start (Part 1) | SilverTaza.com\",\"url\":\"https://silvertaza.com/blog/walling-stair-step-method-1/\"},{\"title\":\"Bootstrapping a Business with the Stair Step Approach — MicroConf\",\"url\":\"https://microconf.com/on-air-episodes/the-stair-step-approach-to-bootstrapping-with-corey-haines\"},{\"title\":\"The low-risk approach to successfully bootstrapping a SaaS - Indie Hackers\",\"url\":\"https://www.indiehackers.com/post/the-low-risk-approach-to-successfully-bootstrapping-a-saas-a0015f7e11\"},{\"title\":\"How I Used The Stairstep Approach To Build My First Product Business - Bean Ninjas\",\"url\":\"https://beanninjas.com/blog/stairstep-method/\"},{\"title\":\"The Bootstrapped Founder | 270: Rob Walling — Stair-Stepping into SaaS Success\",\"url\":\"https://tbf.fm/episodes/270-rob-walling-stair-stepping-into-saas-success\"},{\"title\":\"Stair Step Method - What Is It, Examples, Steps\",\"url\":\"https://www.wallstreetmojo.com/stair-step-method/\"},{\"title\":\"270: Rob Walling — Stair-Stepping into SaaS Success\",\"url\":\"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/270-rob-walling-stair-stepping-into-saas-success/id1497896808?i=1000635686864\"}]\n\nI found information about Rob Walling's Stair Step Approach to bootstrapping SaaS. Here's what the search results reveal:\n\n## The Stair Step Approach Overview\n\nThe Stair Step Approach to Bootstrapping is a method that Rob Walling charted out in 2015 and it has helped thousands of entrepreneurs slowly build their chops online, find a way to buy back their time from an employer, and build a business that creates financial independence.\n\n## The Steps\n\nThe approach starts with small bets on someone else's platform, then you establish reliable revenue stream from all these offers. And then in step three, you build a standalone SaaS business.\n\n**Step 1** focuses on creating a simple product, with a simple marketing plan — one that only requires a single traffic channel. It's much easier to sell an add-on to an existing ecosystem like a WordPress plugin, a Shopify app, a Heroku add-on – they're usually small things to build, relatively inexpensive for customers to purchase, and you have built in discovery through the plugin repository or app store.\n\n**Step 2** involves doubling-down on the model that worked in Step 1 and repeating it until you own your time. You may be able to grow a single product to achieve step 2, or you may need to cobble a few together.\n\n**Step 3** is building a standalone SaaS product. There's a long ramp to any kind of substantial revenue, which is why I recommend you complete steps 1 and 2 before moving to this step.\n\n## Why This Approach Works\n\nThe stairstep approach allows bootstrapped founders to \"level up\" their skills and businesses without giving up control to VCs, incurring debt, or burning out.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8d0f6bac-1fd6-41bf-a61d-b1584e92f748","timestamp":"2026-06-24T02:37:48.690Z",