## Jonathan Stark's \"Hourly Billing Is Nuts\" Philosophy\n\nJonathan Stark is the author of \"Hourly Billing Is Nuts,\" the host of Ditching Hourly, and writes a daily newsletter on pricing for independent professionals. Stark dismantles hourly pricing and breaks down how value-based pricing can lead to higher profits, better clients, and more meaningful work.\n\n## Core Message: Sell Outcomes, Not Hours\n\nStark emphasizes that you need to \"sell your head, not your hands. Your expertise, not your labor. Outcomes, not activities. Benefits, not deliverables.\" The result of value-based pricing is less burnout, better fit with clients, and fees that reflect outcomes—not hours.\n\n## Why Hourly Billing Is Problematic\n\nStark explains that hourly billing \"punishes expertise if you're billing for your time. The better you are, the worse you get paid.\" Hourly billing rewarded inefficiency in his software firm—and clashed with the desire to do high-quality, strategic work.\n\n## His Personal Transformation\n\nStark went solo in 2006 and the first year he basically doubled his income. Instead of \"scoping first\" by diving into project details, Stark focuses on understanding the business outcomes clients want to achieve, gaining insights that help price based on value, not time.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f47d7920-429b-491c-9fa9-4d170dfe1466","timestamp":"2026-06-24T02:38:22.454Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Jonathan Stark \"hourly billing is nuts\" value-based pricing sell outcomes not hours freelance","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01K5QYuoF5LDkG7oojzMEzcA","content":[{"title":"238: Why Hourly Pricing Is A Race to the Bottom (And How to Make More Money) with Jonathan Stark: Part 1","url":"https://successfulfashiondesigner.com/podcast/hourly-pricing-vs-value-pricing-part-1-with-jonathan-stark/"},{"title":"Hourly billing is nuts! - Business Coach Jonathan Stark","url":"https:/